classDiagram
    class Task {
        +String description
        +String time
        +String frequency
        +date due_date
        +bool completed
        +String priority
        +#95;#95;post_init#95;#95;() void
        +mark_complete() void
        +to_dict() dict
        +from_dict(data) Task
    }

    class Pet {
        +String name
        +String breed
        +List~Task~ tasks
        +add_task(task) void
        +remove_task(task) void
        +to_dict() dict
        +from_dict(data) Pet
    }

    class Owner {
        +String name
        +List~Pet~ pets
        +add_pet(pet) void
        +get_all_tasks() List~Task~
        +to_dict() dict
        +from_dict(data) Owner
        +save_to_json(path) void
        +load_from_json(path) Owner
    }

    class Scheduler {
        +Owner owner
        +get_todays_schedule() List~Task~
        +sort_by_time(tasks) List~Task~
        +filter_tasks(pet_name, completed) List~Task~
        +next_available_slot(on, after, step_minutes) String
        +detect_conflicts(suggest) List~String~
        +mark_task_complete(pet, task) Task
    }

    Owner "1" *-- "0..*" Pet : owns
    Pet "1" *-- "0..*" Task : owns
    Scheduler "1" --> "1" Owner : reads tasks via get_all_tasks()
    Scheduler ..> Task : sorts, filters, flags conflicts
    Scheduler ..> Pet : mark_task_complete() adds the next occurrence

    note for Scheduler "Only class that makes scheduling decisions.<br/>Tasks do not store their pet; the Scheduler finds it by walking owner.pets."
    note for Task "#95;#95;post_init#95;#95; normalizes time to HH:MM and raises ValueError for a bad time,<br/>frequency (once, daily, weekly) or priority (low, medium, high)."
    note for Task "Recurrence: completing a daily/weekly task copies it<br/>with due_date = max(due_date, today) + 1 or 7 days."
